<div class="row mt-4">
  <div class="col-md-7 col-lg-8 pe-md-5">
    
    <h4>Paper 2020/341</h4>
    <h3 class="mb-3"><a href="/2020/341.pdf">Faster computation of isogenies of large prime degree</a></h3>
     
    <p class="fst-italic mb-3">
      Daniel J.  Bernstein, Luca De Feo, Antonin Leroux, and Benjamin Smith
    </p>
    
    <h5 class="mt-3">Abstract</h5>
    <p style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Let $\mathcal{E}/\mathbb{F}_q$ be an elliptic curve, and $P$ a point in $\mathcal{E}(\mathbb{F}_q)$ of prime order $\ell$.
Vélu&#39;s formulae let us compute a quotient curve $\mathcal{E}&#39; = \mathcal{E}/\langle{P}\rangle$ and rational maps defining a quotient isogeny $\phi: \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{E}&#39;$ in $\widetilde{O}(\ell)$ $\mathbb{F}_q$-operations, where the $\widetilde{O}$ is uniform in $q$.
This article shows how to compute $\mathcal{E}&#39;$, and $\phi(Q)$ for $Q$ in $\mathcal{E}(\mathbb{F}_q)$, using only $\widetilde{O}(\sqrt{\ell})$ $\mathbb{F}_q$-operations, where the $\widetilde{O}$ is again uniform in $q$.
As an application, this article speeds up some computations used in the isogeny-based cryptosystems CSIDH and CSURF.</p>
  
  </div>
